Z||000000||Punkndrublic||03-02-99||08:39 PM||||I have a 4sp in my 85 GT and i was just wondering which 5sp would be the best(strongest) to put in it with relative easy modifications. I need it to handle high torque and hp.
Z||000001||reecejr||03-03-99||10:09 AM||||I too have a '85 GT and am about 2 weeks ahead of you in answering this question.<p>I ordered the Big Fiero Parts Book. On page ACE-6, it lists transmissions that will fit a Fiero.  The 5-speed Getrag 284 is rated as the highest reliability. It was available in 1991-1993 3.4 TDC V6 motor in a Cutlass, Grand Prix, and Lumina.  Expect to pay BIG BUCKS (approx. $2,000 or more).  The 5-Speed Getrag 282 is rated as high reliability and is much more common.  It was available in 1989-1993 3.1 V6 motors in lots of things - Beretta, Cavaliers, Fierenza, Sunbirds, Pontiac 6000's, etc.<p>I found a Getrag 282 from a 1989 Beretta and am working with Rodney Dickman to convert.  So far, he has been very knowledge and helpful.  He has a conversion kit, and list of additional parts needed to make it work.<p>I plan on installing the tranny over the next few week-ends.  Let me know if you would like progress reports.<p>Hope this helps.
Z||000002||Punkndrublic||03-04-99||06:53 PM||||I would be really interested in hearing about  your progress, especailly any problems you might have. If you need to just email me
Z||000003||theogre||03-30-99||06:17 PM||||Part of the problem with upgrading for high torque is the clutch...... chose your cluch very carefully or it Will die quickly.
